{"authored" [{"question" "q-346057" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${\\int }_{4}^{1}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-3,$ calculate ${\\int }_{1}^{4}(2f(x)+x)\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{4}(2f(x)+x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "e08a60b4d97f3d47007b4efdb7f7fd606625bb3eb2098cf82658b868fe3b7300" "basis" 1106 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-346057" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{4}^{1}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can split up the given integral using the sum rule and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}(2f(x)+x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{1}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,+\\,{\\int }_{1}^{4}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2(3)\\,+\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\,{|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =6\\,+\\,\\frac{16-1}{2} \\\\  & =6\\,+\\,\\frac{15}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "e08a60b4d97f3d47007b4efdb7f7fd606625bb3eb2098cf82658b868fe3b7300" "basis" 1106 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-346057" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0366f23d3812e03904accf1acab42f1872d82ef69e7c77814658267bfe22812" "basis" 1106 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-346057" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "e08a60b4d97f3d47007b4efdb7f7fd606625bb3eb2098cf82658b868fe3b7300" "basis" 1106 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-4797" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose that $f(x)$ is a  function such that ${\\int }_{2}^{-2}\\frac{1}{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-3$ and ${\\int }_{2}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=10.$  What is the value of ${\\int }_{-2}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071258/state.json" "file_sha256" "9359f982db331aeed2de7e0d19bdd053cad3e9476ac6ff317dae0eea70560061"} {"question" "q-4797" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's simplify one of the given integrals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{-2}\\frac{1}{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-3 \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{2}^{-2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-3 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-3 \\\\ {\\int }_{-2}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, from the adjacent intervals rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =12+10 \\\\  & =22.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071258/state.json" "file_sha256" "9359f982db331aeed2de7e0d19bdd053cad3e9476ac6ff317dae0eea70560061"} {"question" "q-4797" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071258/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a77c24f130b0fcd895b6505caef1e295cf3d1e234909f967dfe908bdb0ac0a3e"} {"question" "q-4797" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071258/state.json" "file_sha256" "9359f982db331aeed2de7e0d19bdd053cad3e9476ac6ff317dae0eea70560061"} {"question" "q-4797" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "14"] ["math" "17"] ["math" "20"] ["math" "22"] ["math" "24"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071258/state.json" "file_sha256" "9359f982db331aeed2de7e0d19bdd053cad3e9476ac6ff317dae0eea70560061"} {"question" "q-4797" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "22"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071258/state.json" "file_sha256" "9359f982db331aeed2de7e0d19bdd053cad3e9476ac6ff317dae0eea70560061"} {"question" "q-346043" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${\\int }_{6}^{0}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=4,$ calculate \n${\\int }_{0}^{6}(5f(x)+1)\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{6}(5f(x)+1)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071258/state.json" "file_sha256" "9359f982db331aeed2de7e0d19bdd053cad3e9476ac6ff317dae0eea70560061"} {"question" "q-346043" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{6}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{6}^{0}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can split up the given integral using the sum rule and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{6}(5f(x)+1)\\,\\text{d}x & =5{\\int }_{0}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,+\\,{\\int }_{0}^{6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5(-4)\\,+\\,x\\,{|}_{0}^{6} \\\\  & =-20\\,+\\,(6-0) \\\\  & =-20\\,+\\,6 \\\\  & =-14.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071258/state.json" "file_sha256" "9359f982db331aeed2de7e0d19bdd053cad3e9476ac6ff317dae0eea70560061"} {"question" "q-346043" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071258/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a77c24f130b0fcd895b6505caef1e295cf3d1e234909f967dfe908bdb0ac0a3e"} {"question" "q-346043" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071258/state.json" "file_sha256" "9359f982db331aeed2de7e0d19bdd053cad3e9476ac6ff317dae0eea70560061"} {"question" "q-346043" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-14"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071258/state.json" "file_sha256" "9359f982db331aeed2de7e0d19bdd053cad3e9476ac6ff317dae0eea70560061"} {"question" "q-346057" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${\\int }_{4}^{1}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-3,$ calculate ${\\int }_{1}^{4}(2f(x)+x)\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{4}(2f(x)+x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071258/state.json" "file_sha256" "9359f982db331aeed2de7e0d19bdd053cad3e9476ac6ff317dae0eea70560061"} {"question" "q-346057" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{4}^{1}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can split up the given integral using the sum rule and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}(2f(x)+x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{1}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,+\\,{\\int }_{1}^{4}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2(3)\\,+\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\,{|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =6\\,+\\,\\frac{16-1}{2} \\\\  & =6\\,+\\,\\frac{15}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071258/state.json" "file_sha256" "9359f982db331aeed2de7e0d19bdd053cad3e9476ac6ff317dae0eea70560061"} {"question" "q-346057" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071258/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a77c24f130b0fcd895b6505caef1e295cf3d1e234909f967dfe908bdb0ac0a3e"} {"question" "q-346057" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071258/state.json" "file_sha256" "9359f982db331aeed2de7e0d19bdd053cad3e9476ac6ff317dae0eea70560061"} {"question" "q-346057" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{27}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071258/state.json" "file_sha256" "9359f982db331aeed2de7e0d19bdd053cad3e9476ac6ff317dae0eea70560061"} {"question" "q-346195" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${\\int }_{3}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=0$ and ${\\int }_{7}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=5,$ then what is ${\\int }_{3}^{10}(3f(x)-4)\\,\\text{d}x?$\n\n${\\int }_{3}^{10}(3f(x)-4)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071258/state.json" "file_sha256" "9359f982db331aeed2de7e0d19bdd053cad3e9476ac6ff317dae0eea70560061"} {"question" "q-346195" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the adjacent intervals rule, we know that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{3}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,+\\,{\\int }_{7}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,=\\,{\\int }_{3}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nPlugging in the known information gives\n\n$$\n0+5\\,=\\,{\\int }_{3}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,⇒\\,{\\int }_{3}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=5.\n$$\n\nFinally, compute the desired integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{10}(3f(x)-4)\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{3}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,-\\,4{\\int }_{3}^{10}1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3(5)\\,-\\,4\\cdot x{|}_{3}^{10} \\\\  & =15\\,-\\,4(10-3) \\\\  & =15-28 \\\\  & =-13\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071258/state.json" "file_sha256" "9359f982db331aeed2de7e0d19bdd053cad3e9476ac6ff317dae0eea70560061"} {"question" "q-346195" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071258/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a77c24f130b0fcd895b6505caef1e295cf3d1e234909f967dfe908bdb0ac0a3e"} {"question" "q-346195" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071258/state.json" "file_sha256" "9359f982db331aeed2de7e0d19bdd053cad3e9476ac6ff317dae0eea70560061"} {"question" "q-346195" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-13"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071258/state.json" "file_sha256" "9359f982db331aeed2de7e0d19bdd053cad3e9476ac6ff317dae0eea70560061"} {"question" "q-346219" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose that $f(x)$ is a function such that ${\\int }_{5}^{-1}7\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=14$ and ${\\int }_{-4}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}.$ What is the value of ${\\int }_{-4}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x?$\n\n${\\int }_{-4}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071258/state.json" "file_sha256" "9359f982db331aeed2de7e0d19bdd053cad3e9476ac6ff317dae0eea70560061"} {"question" "q-346219" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's simplify one of the given integrals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{5}^{-1}7\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =14 \\\\ 7{\\int }_{5}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =14 \\\\ -7{\\int }_{-1}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =14 \\\\ {\\int }_{-1}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, from the adjacent intervals rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-4}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+(-2) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071258/state.json" "file_sha256" "9359f982db331aeed2de7e0d19bdd053cad3e9476ac6ff317dae0eea70560061"} {"question" "q-346219" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071258/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a77c24f130b0fcd895b6505caef1e295cf3d1e234909f967dfe908bdb0ac0a3e"} {"question" "q-346219" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071258/state.json" "file_sha256" "9359f982db331aeed2de7e0d19bdd053cad3e9476ac6ff317dae0eea70560061"} {"question" "q-346219" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{3}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071258/state.json" "file_sha256" "9359f982db331aeed2de7e0d19bdd053cad3e9476ac6ff317dae0eea70560061"}] "usage" {"q-346057" []} "basis" 2557 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [17592186287246 17592186287247] "immutable_fields" [[17592186287245 :answer-field/correct] [17592186287245 :answer-field/id] [17592186287245 :answer-field/key] [17592186287245 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
